.TH DIR 1
.SH NAME
dir \- a directory's files as icons or as a list
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/dir
[
.I directory
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Dir
shows the files of
.I directory
(default
.BR / )
in a
.IR wm (1)
window, each as an icon over its name, the first
.B ..
for the directory above.
The icons are
.IR icon (2)'s
glyphs, a folder, a program, a text, source, image, PDF or Markdown file,
an archive, sound or film, painted in the current theme's colours; a
theme switch repaints them.
.PP
Double-clicking button 1 on a folder shows that folder in the same
window, or with
.B "A window for each folder"
checked in the
.B Options
menu, in a new one.
Double-clicking a file plumbs its full name, with the folder as the
working directory; in Lucifer the presentation view takes it, an editor
for text and a viewer for images and documents.
With no plumber running, a program
.RB ( .dis )
runs, an image opens in
.IR view (1),
a PDF in
.IR page (1),
and anything else in
.IR edit (1).
Button 3 plumbs the name it is on.
.PP
The
.B Options
menu sorts the files by name, by when they were last read or written, or
by size, and shows them as icons or as a list of size, time and name.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/dir.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR edit (1),
.IR wm (1),
.IR icon (2),
.IR plumber (8)
